.TH TENSDIFF 1 "31 October 2026" "tenskit @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensdiff \- compare two tensor containers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY tensdiff
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-match\-names ]
.RB [ \-\-fold ]
.RB [ \-\-force\-single\-file ]
.I left
.I right
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tensdiff
compares two containers.
The report lists a format difference, member names only on one side,
and one line for each tensor that differs or was paired under another name.
Metadata keys stay on their own lines.
Comparison continues after the first mismatch.
.PP
A tensor line is
.IR "name : dtype : shape" .
.B =>
appears only on a field that differs, so a shared dtype or shape is written once.
When the dtype and shape match and the bytes do not, the line ends with
.IR "values differ at byte N" .
A renamed pair whose dtype, shape, and bytes match is printed and does not
by itself make the exit status 1.
Tensor lines and names only on one side are sorted by name.
A run of digits compares as a number, so
.I .10.
follows
.IR .9. .
.PP
A dtype match uses the canonical id, so
.I F32
and
.I float32
are the same type.
A GGUF shape is reversed from
.I ne[]
before it is compared.
The bytes compared are the logical tensor:
GGUF alignment padding is dropped, and a quantized tensor is the block bytes,
not a dequantized float.
.PP
A directory is the safetensors weight set, the same rule as
.BR \%tenspile (1).
A
.I .safetensors
file beside
.I config.json
is refused unless
.B \-\-force\-single\-file
is written immediately before that path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the same findings as one document.
.B \-\-fold
does not apply to
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-match\-names
Pair names that differ through the GGUF role table.
A GGUF
.I \%general.architecture
value selects that architecture.
Otherwise every architecture is tried, and the smallest role set that
explains every remaining name wins.
When several architectures still fit, the report says
.IR "names: may be A, B, or C" .
Each pair lists both names.
.I language_model.
is removed before the lookup.
Vision and audio tensors are left unpaired in a language file.
Qwen3.5
.I dt_bias
and
.I mtp.*
names use the rewrites in
.IR \%qwen35_tensor_names_to_gguf .
If nothing covers the names, the report says
.I names: no table matched
and falls back to exact names.
Paired Q and K weights stay in the order stored in the file.
.TP
.B \-\-fold
Merge tensor lines that are the same except for one consecutive number.
A number that advances on both sides is written as a range on both sides.
A number that stays the same is written once.
A gap is not bridged.
.I blk.20
and
.I blk.21
become
.IR blk.[20\-21] .
.TP
.BI \-\-force\-single\-file " path"
Read this
.I .safetensors
file even when
.I config.json
is in the same directory.
It applies only to the path written immediately after it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the short help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The format, names, types, shapes, values, and metadata match.
.TP
.B 1
A difference was printed.
A different container format counts, so a file and its conversion exit 1
even when every tensor matches; the report then has only its
.I format:
line.
.TP
.B 2
A file could not be read, or the command line was not valid.
The message is written to stderr and starts with
.BR "\%tensdiff: " .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compare two files of any formats:
.RS
.EX
tensdiff before.safetensors after.safetensors
.EE
.RE
.PP
Check a conversion: only the format line is printed when every tensor matches.
.RS
.EX
tensconv \-o model.pt model.safetensors
tensdiff model.safetensors model.pt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Compare a Hugging Face checkpoint with its GGUF conversion, pairing the names and folding the layers:
.RS
.EX
tensdiff \-\-match\-names \-\-fold model/ model.gguf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Get the findings as JSON:
.RS
.EX
tensdiff \-\-json left.npz right.npz
.EE
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
Nick Reynolds (goldnode)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR \%tenspile (1),
.BR \%tensinfo (1),
.BR \%tensconv (1),
.BR \%tensquant (1)
